{"chunk_id": "5d7507b13211", "text": "Bhishma recounts an ancient revelation about Vasudeva (Krishna). Brahma prays to the Supreme Lord\u2014source even of Brahma himself\u2014to incarnate among humans to destroy the Asuras reborn on Earth and restore cosmic order. The Lord agrees through the power of Yoga and disappears. When the gods ask who was addressed with such reverence, Brahma explains that the being is the eternal, unmanifest Supreme Self\u2014Vasudeva\u2014beyond beginning and end, the refuge of all existence. He foretells that the divine sages Nara and Narayana will appear among men and remain unrecognized by the ignorant. Bhishma concludes that Krishna is this supreme reality and that wherever Krishna and righteousness stand, victory must follow\u2014hence the Pandavas will inevitably triumph.\nBhishma recounts Brahma\u2019s revelation that the supreme Vasudeva will incarnate among humans to destroy Asuras and support the Pandavas, affirming Krishna\u2019s divine supremacy.\nThemes: divine incarnation, Krishna's supremacy, cosmic order and dharma, prophecy of victory, devotion to Vasudeva", "vector": [0.005924461875110865, -0.012847834266722202, -0.012414096854627132, 0.011461189016699791, -0.018282698467373848, 0.016100866720080376, -0.02077997662127018, -0.029257575049996376, -0.021989183500409126, 0.005448007490485907, 0.014760223217308521, 0.006486349273473024, -0.0032300311140716076, 0.010304555296897888, -0.004590390250086784, -0.0016922339564189315, 0.038694653660058975, -0.010048255324363708, 0.022580644115805626, -0.0036900558043271303, 0.016442598775029182, -0.012446955777704716, 0.009673663415014744, 0.012262945994734764, -0.023829283192753792, 0.006532351952046156, 0.03057193197309971, -0.021713169291615486, 0.014300198294222355, -0.02994104102253914, -0.004915693309158087, 0.00784013606607914, -0.0014638645807281137, 0.004133651033043861, -0.01670547015964985, 0.0067295050248503685, -0.007123812101781368, -0.01531225349754095, 0.018046114593